{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And He called to Moses.</b> Midrash Tanchuma: Because Moses was standing outside, for he was afraid to enter the Tent of Meeting since the cloud was upon it, the Holy One, blessed be He, said: It is only right that Moses should stand outside! Immediately, ״ויקרא אל משה״. And Rashi comments: for all the divine utterances and for all the sayings, etc. And further Rashi comments: Could it be that all Israel heard the voice of the call? It is written: ״קול לו״ — 'a voice to him.' This means, according to his interpretation, that it is written in the portion of נשא: ״וישמע את הקול מדבר אליו״, and it should have said 'speaking to him' or 'with him'; but since it writes 'to him,' it implies a restriction — 'to him,' to Moses: Moses hears, but Israel does not hear."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:47.318011335Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}